{#-
  One chapter — SPEC.md §11, §12, §13, §17, §18.

  Two shapes for the same content, chosen by `commentary.mode`:

  * `inline` — the commentary sits in the reading flow. Structure follows §13, which
    supersedes §12.2's whole-unit wrapper: only a small `keep-together` block (verse +
    divider + first entry) carries the page-break hint. Kindle ignores the hint entirely,
    and readers that honour it would otherwise leave a blank page before a Rashi that runs
    for several screens.

  * `details` — the commentary is collapsed until the reader taps רש״י, so the biblical
    text runs continuously. Native HTML5 `<details>`/`<summary>`, no JavaScript (§26, §36).
    `<summary>` takes over the divider's job, so it keeps the divider's classes. The
    `keep-together` wrapper is dropped here: there is nothing to hold beside the verse when
    the commentary starts closed.

  Both keep the same verse and commentary-entry structure, so nothing downstream — ids,
  anchors, navigation — changes with the mode.

  The verse and each commentary entry arrive as internal markup that markup.py has already
  escaped; every other value is autoescaped by Jinja.
-#}
{%- import "_macros.xhtml.j2" as m -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:epub="http://www.idpf.org/2007/ops"
      xml:lang="he" lang="he" dir="rtl">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <title>{{ page_title }}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../styles/main.css"/>
</head>
<body dir="rtl">
  <section id="{{ chapter_anchor }}" epub:type="chapter"{% if book_start %} class="book-start"{% endif %}>
{%- if book_start %}
    <h1 class="book-heading">{{ book_hebrew_title }}</h1>
{%- endif %}
    <h2 class="chapter-heading">{{ chapter_label }}</h2>
{%- for unit in units %}
    <section class="study-unit">
{%- if collapsible %}
      {{ m.verse(unit) }}
      {%- if unit.commentary %}
      <details class="commentary {{ unit.commentary.slug }}" id="{{ unit.commentary_id }}">
        <summary class="commentary-divider {{ unit.commentary.slug }}-divider">{{ unit.commentary.hebrew }}</summary>
        {%- for entry in unit.commentary.entries %}
        {{ m.commentary_entry(entry, unit.commentary.slug) }}
        {%- endfor %}
      </details>
      {%- endif %}
{%- else %}
      <div class="keep-together">
        {{ m.verse(unit) }}
        {%- if unit.commentary %}
        <div class="commentary-divider {{ unit.commentary.slug }}-divider">{{ unit.commentary.hebrew }}</div>
        {{ m.commentary_entry(unit.commentary.entries[0], unit.commentary.slug) }}
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- if unit.commentary and unit.commentary.entries|length > 1 %}
      <section class="commentary {{ unit.commentary.slug }}">
        {%- for entry in unit.commentary.entries[1:] %}
        {{ m.commentary_entry(entry, unit.commentary.slug) }}
        {%- endfor %}
      </section>
      {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
    </section>
{%- endfor %}
  </section>
</body>
</html>
